{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01ACr336oDqqPBH1W5LBZPW8","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t=== kits/README.md\n2\t# The genre kits (v0.85.2)\n3\t\n4\tA kit is a complete small game in one genre, written to be copied: its title, play and end, the modules it rests on,\n5\tits sound, touch controls and a phone's screen. The API card's Genre playbook (`API.md`) names a kit for each genre (its\n6\t\"Copy slice\" column); the table says which file is which. Each kit is the same game as the single-file kit on the site\n7\t(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/kits/<id>), readable, on this package's engine.\n8\t\n9\t- **`<id>.js`**, its game: the starter's shell (the title menu, the keys every kit shares, the proof), the slice, and the\n10\t  start, as the single-file kit holds them between `GAME START` and `GAME END`. Its header says what it plays, its keys,\n11\t  its deep links and how it works.\n12\t- **`<id>.html`** plays it (open it, or `node tools/check.mjs kits/<id>.html#<id>`); `#<id>` starts the slice, and\n13\t  `#<id>/<part>` jumps into a part.\n14\t- **`node kits/test.mjs <id>`** runs it headless: the slice plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice.\n15\t\n16\t**Start a game from one:** copy `<id>.js` to `game/game.js` (and, if its page loads an asset set, that `<script>` line into\n17\t`game/index.html` before `game.js`). Then replace the starter's title menu with your own title scene and keep only your\n18\tgame, as its header says. Its test: copy `kits/test.mjs`'s three stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`) into\n19\t`game/test.mjs`. A game of several genres reads the kits it mixes and builds on the full engine, which has every module.\n20\t\n21\t| Kit | Files | What it plays | Modules | Deep links |\n22\t| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n23\t| ADVENTURE | [adventure.js](adventure.js), [adventure.html](adventure.html) | a top-down action adventure: a village, ruins and a shrine, a sword, a key and a great door, talk with portraits; Zelda and Secret of Mana | none | #adventure |\n24\t| POINT-AND-CLICK | [pointclick.js](pointclick.js), [pointclick.html](pointclick.html) | an adventure of three rooms: a dock, a tavern, a lighthouse; four puzzles, the nine verbs or a verb coin, an inventory, a riddle contest | click, story | #pointclick |\n25\t| PLATFORMER | [platformer.js](platformer.js), [platformer.html](platformer.html) | a side-scroller: a night approach to a castle in five zones, a sword, a dash, candles, a 2.5D view; Castlevania, Mega Man X, Klonoa | none | #platformer |\n26\t| METROIDVANIA | [metroidvania.js](metroidvania.js), [metroidvania.html](metroidvania.html) | a world of rooms: its map, two abilities that open its gates, a save room, two bosses | rooms | #metroidvania, #metroidvania/miniboss, #metroidvania/boss, #metroidvania/map |\n27\t| SHOOTER | [shooter.js](shooter.js), [shooter.html](shooter.html) | a vertical shoot-'em-up stage, then a horizontal one: waves, power-ups, bosses; 1943 and Raiden, then Gradius and R-Type | arcade | #shooter, #shooter/horizontal |\n28\t| ARCADE | [arcade.js](arcade.js), [arcade.html](arcade.html) | a cabinet of three: maze, formation, rocks | arcade, grid, gen | #arcade, #arcade/maze, #arcade/formation, #arcade/rocks |\n29\t| PINBALL | [pinball.js](pinball.js), [pinball.html](pinball.html) | one table: flippers, bumpers, a ramp, drop targets, a spinner, a kickback, a mission, multiball, tilt, a dot-matrix display | physics, arcade | #pinball |\n30\t| ARTILLERY | [artillery.js](artillery.js), [artillery.html](artillery.html) | two teams of three on an island every blast carves: turns, aim and power, wind, a rocket, a bouncing grenade, a cluster bomb, falls and the sea, a CPU that tries its shots in simulation | physics, terrain, grid | #artillery, #artillery/cpu |\n31\t| PUZZLE | [puzzle.js](puzzle.js), [puzzle.html](puzzle.html) | falling blocks and falling pairs that chain, versus with a second player or the CPU; Tetris, Puyo Puyo | grid | #puzzle |\n32\t| RHYTHM | [rhythm.js](rhythm.js), [rhythm.html](rhythm.html) | four lanes on the music clock: two songs, notes, jumps, holds, a rapping teacher to answer, a dancer and a crowd on the beat, grades, the audio offset | songs, rhythm | #rhythm, #rhythm/stepup, #rhythm/rapschool, #rhythm/calibrate |\n33\t| RPG | [rpg.js](rpg.js), [rpg.html](rpg.html) | a JRPG's journey: a town, a world map, a cave and its boss, the ATB battle, menus and save slots | story, rpg | #rpg, #rpg/battle |\n34\t| ROGUELIKE | [roguelike.js](roguelike.js), [roguelike.html](roguelike.html) | a turn-based crypt of ten generated floors: fields of view and fog, turns by speed, potions and scrolls; Rogue, Mystery Dungeon | grid, gen | #roguelike |\n35\t| TACTICS | [tactics.js](tactics.js), [tactics.html](tactics.html) | an isometric battle on a map of heights: charge time or phases, facing, arcs, areas, a scoring AI | grid, story | #tactics, #tactics/battle, #tactics/phases |\n36\t| RTS | [rts.js](rts.js), [rts.html](rts.html) | real-time strategy: workers, gold, a barracks and a stable, three kinds to fight, fog, an enemy camp that builds and attacks in waves | grid, strategy | #rts |\n37\t| SIM | [sim.js](sim.js), [sim.html](sim.html) | a theme park: paths, four rides and two shops, guests with needs and money, prices, a rating, day and night, time controls | grid, strategy | #sim |\n38\t| BRAWLER | [brawler.js](brawler.js), [brawler.html](brawler.html) | a beat-'em-up: a city block at dusk, combos, grabs and kicks, waves that lock the screen, a second player who drops in; Final Fight, Streets of Rage | none | #brawler |\n39\t| FIGHTING | [fighting.js](fighting.js), [fighting.html](fighting.html) | one on one: three fighters, versus, arcade, training | fight | #fighting, #fighting/versus, #fighting/arcade, #fighting/training |\n40\t| ANIMATION LAB | [animlab.js](animlab.js), [animlab.html](animlab.html) | every move, pose, skin and view of the character rigs | none | #animlab |\n41\t| KART | [kart.js](kart.js), [kart.html](kart.html) | Mode 7 karts: six on a circuit, three laps, items, two players in a split screen | mode7, drive | #kart, #kart/race, #kart/vs |\n42\t| ROAD | [road.js](road.js), [road.html](road.html) | a pseudo-3D coast road against the clock: curves, hills, a tunnel, traffic, checkpoints, a radio | road | #road, #road/drive |\n43\t| SPORTS | [sports.js](sports.js), [sports.html](sports.html) | two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam | none | #sports, #sports/match, #sports/vs |\n44\t| STEALTH | [stealth.js](stealth.js), [stealth.html](stealth.html) | third-person stealth and parkour: a rooftop district at dusk, guards with sight and suspicion, climbing, takedowns, an HTML HUD; Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear | none | #stealth |\n45\t\n46\t**3D:** the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows, are not in this package. They are on the\n47\tsite (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d, /kits/3d-<genre>) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge:\n48\t`engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js`, its header the 3D manual; `src/starter3d/`). Here, a 3D game is built on the 2D engine's views,\n49\ta world in x, y and z drawn from any angle (`API.md`, Coordinates).\n50\t=== game/index.html\n51\t<!doctype html>\n52\t<html lang=\"en\">\n53\t<head>\n54\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n55\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n56\t<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\n57\t<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n58\t</head>\n59\t<body>\n60\t<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.2</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n61\t<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n62\t<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n63\t<script src=\"game.js\"></script>\n64\t</body>\n65\t</html>\n66\t=== kits/sports.html\n67\t<!doctype html>\n68\t<html lang=\"en\">\n69\t<head>\n70\t<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n71\t<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n72\t<title>SPORTS · my-3D2dge kit</title>\n73\t<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n74\t</head>\n75\t<body>\n76\t<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">SPORTS</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.2</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n77\t<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n78\t<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n79\t<script src=\"sports.js\"></script>\n80\t</body>\n81\t</html>\n82\t=== game/test.mjs\n83\t// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n84\t// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n85\t// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\n86\timport vm from 'node:vm';\n87\timport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n88\t\n89\tconst ctx = { console };\n90\tvm.createContext(ctx);\n91\tfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\n92\tconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\n93\tlet failed = 0;\n94\tconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n95\t\n96\tgame.advance(.5);\n97\tcheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n98\tI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\n99\tcheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n100\t\n101\t// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n102\t// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\n103\tgame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\n104\tI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\n105\tcheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n106\tI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\n107\tcheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n108\t\n109\t// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\n110\tgame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\n111\tcheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n112\tgame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\n113\tcheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n114\t\n115\t// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\n116\tI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\n117\tconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\n118\tgame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\n119\tgame.advance(2.5);\n120\tcheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n121\tcheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n122\t\n123\tconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\n124\tprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n125\t=== kits/test.mjs\n126\t// A headless test of the genre kits: each kit's game runs in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where there is no\n127\t// DOM) after the scripts its page loads before it (the engine, an asset set), starts its slice (the page's deep link,\n128\t// #<id>), plays two seconds, then runs the slice's proof twice: run(600), scripted play from a seed, gives a hash of how\n129\t// it went, the same every time. Run it: node kits/test.mjs [id ...] (every kit without one; exit code 1 on a failure).\n130\t// A game copied from a kit tests the same way: a kit's code reads three of the page's globals, given stand-ins here\n131\t// (window, addEventListener, location); drive it with game.advance and input.tap / hold, as game/test.mjs does.\n132\timport vm from 'node:vm';\n133\timport { readFileSync, readdirSync } from 'node:fs';\n134\t\n135\tconst here = new URL('./', import.meta.url), read = f => readFileSync(new URL(f, here), 'utf8');\n136\tconst ids = process.argv.slice(2).length ? process.argv.slice(2) : readdirSync(here).filter(f => f.endsWith('.html')).map(f => f.slice(0, -5)).sort();\n137\tlet failed = 0;\n138\tfor (const id of ids) {\n139\t  const ctx = { console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error: console.error }, addEventListener() {}, location: { hash: '#' + id } };\n140\t  ctx.window = ctx; vm.createContext(ctx);\n141\t  try {\n142\t    // the page's scripts, in its order: ../my-3d2dge.js, any asset set, then the kit's game\n143\t    for (const [, src] of read(id + '.html').matchAll(/<script src=\"([^\"]+)\"><\\/script>/g)) vm.runInContext(read(src), ctx, { filename: src });\n144\t    const game = ctx.My3D2dge.current, slice = ctx.__game.scenes[id];\n145\t    game.advance(2);\n146\t    const scene = game.sceneName, a = slice.run(600), b = slice.run(600), errors = game.errors.map(e => e.message), ok = a === b && !errors.length;\n147\t    console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + id + ': ' + scene + ' plays; its proof twice ' + (a === b ? 'the same (' + a + ')' : a + ', then ' + b) + (errors.length ? '; errors: ' + errors.join(' | ') : ''));\n148\t    if (!ok) failed++;\n149\t  } catch (e) { console.log('FAIL ' + id + ': ' + (e && e.stack || e).toString().split('\\n').slice(0, 3).join(' / ')); failed++; }\n150\t}\n151\tconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} of ${ids.length} kit(s) failed` : `all ${ids.length} kit(s) passed`);\n152\tprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n153\t=== package.json\n154\t{\n155\t  \"name\": \"my-3d2dge-handoff\",\n156\t  \"version\": \"0.85.2\",\n157\t  \"private\": true,\n158\t  \"type\": \"module\",\n159\t  \"description\": \"my-3D2dge for coding agents: the engine, its card, index and guide, the tools and a template game\",\n160\t  \"scripts\": {\n161\t    \"test\": \"node game/test.mjs\",\n162\t    \"check\": \"node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\"\n163\t  },\n164\t  \"devDependencies\": {\n165\t    \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\"\n166\t  }\n167\t}\n168\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eca6c66-8849-4edb-a442-cc89add0a71e","uuid":"b92371e9-3e6d-4e0b-88d3-1113b1ef181d","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:33.571Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/cc-plan-x4394d1/out/r2.txt","content":"=== kits/README.md\n# The genre kits (v0.85.2)\n\nA kit is a complete small game in one genre, written to be copied: its title, play and end, the modules it rests on,\nits sound, touch controls and a phone's screen. The API card's Genre playbook (`API.md`) names a kit for each genre (its\n\"Copy slice\" column); the table says which file is which. Each kit is the same game as the single-file kit on the site\n(my-3d2dge.vercel.app/kits/<id>), readable, on this package's engine.\n\n- **`<id>.js`**, its game: the starter's shell (the title menu, the keys every kit shares, the proof), the slice, and the\n  start, as the single-file kit holds them between `GAME START` and `GAME END`. Its header says what it plays, its keys,\n  its deep links and how it works.\n- **`<id>.html`** plays it (open it, or `node tools/check.mjs kits/<id>.html#<id>`); `#<id>` starts the slice, and\n  `#<id>/<part>` jumps into a part.\n- **`node kits/test.mjs <id>`** runs it headless: the slice plays, and its proof gives the same hash twice.\n\n**Start a game from one:** copy `<id>.js` to `game/game.js` (and, if its page loads an asset set, that `<script>` line into\n`game/index.html` before `game.js`). Then replace the starter's title menu with your own title scene and keep only your\ngame, as its header says. Its test: copy `kits/test.mjs`'s three stand-ins (`window`, `addEventListener`, `location`) into\n`game/test.mjs`. A game of several genres reads the kits it mixes and builds on the full engine, which has every module.\n\n| Kit | Files | What it plays | Modules | Deep links |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| ADVENTURE | [adventure.js](adventure.js), [adventure.html](adventure.html) | a top-down action adventure: a village, ruins and a shrine, a sword, a key and a great door, talk with portraits; Zelda and Secret of Mana | none | #adventure |\n| POINT-AND-CLICK | [pointclick.js](pointclick.js), [pointclick.html](pointclick.html) | an adventure of three rooms: a dock, a tavern, a lighthouse; four puzzles, the nine verbs or a verb coin, an inventory, a riddle contest | click, story | #pointclick |\n| PLATFORMER | [platformer.js](platformer.js), [platformer.html](platformer.html) | a side-scroller: a night approach to a castle in five zones, a sword, a dash, candles, a 2.5D view; Castlevania, Mega Man X, Klonoa | none | #platformer |\n| METROIDVANIA | [metroidvania.js](metroidvania.js), [metroidvania.html](metroidvania.html) | a world of rooms: its map, two abilities that open its gates, a save room, two bosses | rooms | #metroidvania, #metroidvania/miniboss, #metroidvania/boss, #metroidvania/map |\n| SHOOTER | [shooter.js](shooter.js), [shooter.html](shooter.html) | a vertical shoot-'em-up stage, then a horizontal one: waves, power-ups, bosses; 1943 and Raiden, then Gradius and R-Type | arcade | #shooter, #shooter/horizontal |\n| ARCADE | [arcade.js](arcade.js), [arcade.html](arcade.html) | a cabinet of three: maze, formation, rocks | arcade, grid, gen | #arcade, #arcade/maze, #arcade/formation, #arcade/rocks |\n| PINBALL | [pinball.js](pinball.js), [pinball.html](pinball.html) | one table: flippers, bumpers, a ramp, drop targets, a spinner, a kickback, a mission, multiball, tilt, a dot-matrix display | physics, arcade | #pinball |\n| ARTILLERY | [artillery.js](artillery.js), [artillery.html](artillery.html) | two teams of three on an island every blast carves: turns, aim and power, wind, a rocket, a bouncing grenade, a cluster bomb, falls and the sea, a CPU that tries its shots in simulation | physics, terrain, grid | #artillery, #artillery/cpu |\n| PUZZLE | [puzzle.js](puzzle.js), [puzzle.html](puzzle.html) | falling blocks and falling pairs that chain, versus with a second player or the CPU; Tetris, Puyo Puyo | grid | #puzzle |\n| RHYTHM | [rhythm.js](rhythm.js), [rhythm.html](rhythm.html) | four lanes on the music clock: two songs, notes, jumps, holds, a rapping teacher to answer, a dancer and a crowd on the beat, grades, the audio offset | songs, rhythm | #rhythm, #rhythm/stepup, #rhythm/rapschool, #rhythm/calibrate |\n| RPG | [rpg.js](rpg.js), [rpg.html](rpg.html) | a JRPG's journey: a town, a world map, a cave and its boss, the ATB battle, menus and save slots | story, rpg | #rpg, #rpg/battle |\n| ROGUELIKE | [roguelike.js](roguelike.js), [roguelike.html](roguelike.html) | a turn-based crypt of ten generated floors: fields of view and fog, turns by speed, potions and scrolls; Rogue, Mystery Dungeon | grid, gen | #roguelike |\n| TACTICS | [tactics.js](tactics.js), [tactics.html](tactics.html) | an isometric battle on a map of heights: charge time or phases, facing, arcs, areas, a scoring AI | grid, story | #tactics, #tactics/battle, #tactics/phases |\n| RTS | [rts.js](rts.js), [rts.html](rts.html) | real-time strategy: workers, gold, a barracks and a stable, three kinds to fight, fog, an enemy camp that builds and attacks in waves | grid, strategy | #rts |\n| SIM | [sim.js](sim.js), [sim.html](sim.html) | a theme park: paths, four rides and two shops, guests with needs and money, prices, a rating, day and night, time controls | grid, strategy | #sim |\n| BRAWLER | [brawler.js](brawler.js), [brawler.html](brawler.html) | a beat-'em-up: a city block at dusk, combos, grabs and kicks, waves that lock the screen, a second player who drops in; Final Fight, Streets of Rage | none | #brawler |\n| FIGHTING | [fighting.js](fighting.js), [fighting.html](fighting.html) | one on one: three fighters, versus, arcade, training | fight | #fighting, #fighting/versus, #fighting/arcade, #fighting/training |\n| ANIMATION LAB | [animlab.js](animlab.js), [animlab.html](animlab.html) | every move, pose, skin and view of the character rigs | none | #animlab |\n| KART | [kart.js](kart.js), [kart.html](kart.html) | Mode 7 karts: six on a circuit, three laps, items, two players in a split screen | mode7, drive | #kart, #kart/race, #kart/vs |\n| ROAD | [road.js](road.js), [road.html](road.html) | a pseudo-3D coast road against the clock: curves, hills, a tunnel, traffic, checkpoints, a radio | road | #road, #road/drive |\n| SPORTS | [sports.js](sports.js), [sports.html](sports.html) | two against two in a walled cage, up to four players: a ball that bounces and curls, passes, lobs, shots on a meter, formations, a match clock; Sensible Soccer and NBA Jam | none | #sports, #sports/match, #sports/vs |\n| STEALTH | [stealth.js](stealth.js), [stealth.html](stealth.html) | third-person stealth and parkour: a rooftop district at dusk, guards with sight and suspicion, climbing, takedowns, an HTML HUD; Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear | none | #stealth |\n\n**3D:** the 3D engine (three.js and Rapier) and its kits, the playbook's 3D rows, are not in this package. They are on the\nsite (my-3d2dge.vercel.app/3d, /kits/3d-<genre>) and in the repository (github.com/michaelcrosato/my-3d2dge:\n`engine/my-3d2dge-3d.js`, its header the 3D manual; `src/starter3d/`). Here, a 3D game is built on the 2D engine's views,\na world in x, y and z drawn from any angle (`API.md`, Coordinates).\n=== game/index.html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>Rooftop · my-3D2dge template</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">ROOFTOP</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.2</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"game.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n=== kits/sports.html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"utf-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1, viewport-fit=cover\">\n<title>SPORTS · my-3D2dge kit</title>\n<style>html, body { margin: 0; height: 100%; background: #000; overflow: hidden } #screen { width: 100%; height: 100%; display: block; image-rendering: pixelated; touch-action: none }</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n<div id=\"e3-boot\" role=\"status\" style=\"position:fixed;inset:0;z-index:40;display:flex;flex-direction:column;justify-content:flex-end;gap:6px;padding:20px;background:#05040a;color:#a9a1c8;font:12px/1.5 ui-monospace,Menlo,Consolas,monospace\"><style>@keyframes e3-run{from{transform:translateX(-100%)}to{transform:translateX(340%)}}@keyframes e3-late{to{opacity:1}}</style><b style=\"color:#f4f0ff;font-size:16px;letter-spacing:.08em\">SPORTS</b><span>Starting · my-3D2dge v0.85.2</span><span style=\"display:block;height:4px;max-width:440px;overflow:hidden;background:#ffffff14\"><span style=\"display:block;width:30%;height:100%;background:#d9b77c;animation:e3-run 1.2s ease-in-out infinite\"></span></span><span style=\"opacity:0;animation:e3-late .3s 12s forwards\">Still starting. If this stays, the game's script did not run: reload, or open the browser's console.</span></div>\n<canvas id=\"screen\"></canvas>\n<script src=\"../my-3d2dge.js\"></script>\n<script src=\"sports.js\"></script>\n</body>\n</html>\n=== game/test.mjs\n// A headless test of the template game: the engine and game.js run in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where\n// there is no DOM), driven by fixed steps (game.advance) and scripted input (input.tap, input.hold), and read through\n// game.debug.snapshot(). Run it: node game/test.mjs (exit code 1 on a failure). Write one like it for your game.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst ctx = { console };\nvm.createContext(ctx);\nfor (const f of ['../my-3d2dge.js', './game.js']) vm.runInContext(readFileSync(new URL(f, import.meta.url), 'utf8'), ctx, { filename: f });\nconst E = ctx.My3D2dge, game = E.current, I = game.input, snap = () => game.debug.snapshot();\nlet failed = 0;\nconst check = (what, ok, detail = '') => { console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + what + (ok ? '' : ': ' + detail)); if (!ok) failed++; };\n\ngame.advance(.5);\ncheck('the title waits for start', snap().scene === 'title', JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('start begins play', snap().scene === 'play', JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// climb: stand facing the roof's west wall (cells 7-9 of rows 4-6: x 112-160, y 64-112), press jump to take hold, then\n// climb with up (up the screen is up the wall) until it pulls up onto the top\ngame.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0);\nI.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('jump next to a wall takes hold of it', snap().climbing, JSON.stringify(snap()));\nI.hold('up'); game.advance(.6); I.hold('up', false); game.advance(1);\ncheck('climbing up pulls up onto the roof', !snap().climbing && snap().hero[2] === 32, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// take the gem (on the roof's middle cell), then hop down into the street with it\ngame.debug.teleport(136, 88, 32, 0); game.advance(.1);\ncheck('walking onto the gem takes it', snap().got, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ngame.debug.teleport(156, 120, 32, Math.PI / 2); I.hold('down'); game.advance(1.5); I.hold('down', false); game.advance(.5);\ncheck('back in the street with the gem wins', snap().scene === 'end' && snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\n\n// get seen: stand in front of the guard, in the open, until its alert fills\nI.tap('start'); game.advance(.5);\nconst [gx, gy, gf] = snap().guard;\ngame.debug.teleport(gx + Math.cos(gf) * 40, gy + Math.sin(gf) * 40, 0, gf + Math.PI);\ngame.advance(2.5);\ncheck('the guard catches a hero it sees', snap().scene === 'end' && !snap().won, JSON.stringify(snap()));\ncheck('no errors', !game.errors.length, game.errors.map(e => e.message).join(' | '));\n\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} check(s) failed` : 'all checks passed');\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n=== kits/test.mjs\n// A headless test of the genre kits: each kit's game runs in Node with no screen (new E.Game is headless where there is no\n// DOM) after the scripts its page loads before it (the engine, an asset set), starts its slice (the page's deep link,\n// #<id>), plays two seconds, then runs the slice's proof twice: run(600), scripted play from a seed, gives a hash of how\n// it went, the same every time. Run it: node kits/test.mjs [id ...] (every kit without one; exit code 1 on a failure).\n// A game copied from a kit tests the same way: a kit's code reads three of the page's globals, given stand-ins here\n// (window, addEventListener, location); drive it with game.advance and input.tap / hold, as game/test.mjs does.\nimport vm from 'node:vm';\nimport { readFileSync, readdirSync } from 'node:fs';\n\nconst here = new URL('./', import.meta.url), read = f => readFileSync(new URL(f, here), 'utf8');\nconst ids = process.argv.slice(2).length ? process.argv.slice(2) : readdirSync(here).filter(f => f.endsWith('.html')).map(f => f.slice(0, -5)).sort();\nlet failed = 0;\nfor (const id of ids) {\n  const ctx = { console: { log() {}, info() {}, warn() {}, error: console.error }, addEventListener() {}, location: { hash: '#' + id } };\n  ctx.window = ctx; vm.createContext(ctx);\n  try {\n    // the page's scripts, in its order: ../my-3d2dge.js, any asset set, then the kit's game\n    for (const [, src] of read(id + '.html').matchAll(/<script src=\"([^\"]+)\"><\\/script>/g)) vm.runInContext(read(src), ctx, { filename: src });\n    const game = ctx.My3D2dge.current, slice = ctx.__game.scenes[id];\n    game.advance(2);\n    const scene = game.sceneName, a = slice.run(600), b = slice.run(600), errors = game.errors.map(e => e.message), ok = a === b && !errors.length;\n    console.log((ok ? 'ok   ' : 'FAIL ') + id + ': ' + scene + ' plays; its proof twice ' + (a === b ? 'the same (' + a + ')' : a + ', then ' + b) + (errors.length ? '; errors: ' + errors.join(' | ') : ''));\n    if (!ok) failed++;\n  } catch (e) { console.log('FAIL ' + id + ': ' + (e && e.stack || e).toString().split('\\n').slice(0, 3).join(' / ')); failed++; }\n}\nconsole.log(failed ? `${failed} of ${ids.length} kit(s) failed` : `all ${ids.length} kit(s) passed`);\nprocess.exit(failed ? 1 : 0);\n=== package.json\n{\n  \"name\": \"my-3d2dge-handoff\",\n  \"version\": \"0.85.2\",\n  \"private\": true,\n  \"type\": \"module\",\n  \"description\": \"my-3D2dge for coding agents: the engine, its card, index and guide, the tools and a template game\",\n  \"scripts\": {\n    \"test\": \"node game/test.mjs\",\n    \"check\": \"node tools/check.mjs game/index.html\"\n  },\n  \"devDependencies\": {\n    \"playwright\": \"1.63.0\"\n  }\n}\n","numLines":168,"startLine":1,"totalLines":168}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01ACr336oDqqPBH1W5LBZPW8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
