{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017uxjjKQLBkTaFFQB5uN6FH","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n2\t7:## North star\n3\t17:## The mental model\n4\t29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n5\t44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n6\t64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n7\t72:## Hard rules\n8\t82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n9\t120:## Frame order\n10\t140:## Systems in more depth\n11\t142:### Views and resolution\n12\t150:### Scenes\n13\t155:### Camera\n14\t163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n15\t169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n16\t178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n17\t190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n18\t222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n19\t242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n20\t249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n21\t255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n22\t267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n23\t273:### Attack (melee timing)\n24\t280:### Bullets and patterns\n25\t286:### Humanoid\n26\t297:### Audio\n27\t305:### Text and UI\n28\t311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n29\t319:### Lighting\n30\t328:### Errors and warnings\n31\t338:### Testing without a browser\n32\t357:### The handoff package\n33\t360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n34\t367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n35\t374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n36\t402:## Genre recipes\n37\t606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n38\t631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n39\t648:## Performance\n40\t656:## Checklist before handing a game back\n41\t===\n42\t41:6. **Tune the feel** with the feel numbers in `API.md`, then check the game with the skeleton overlay (`rig.debug(r)`) and in slow motion (`game.timeScale = .25`).\n43\t101:    controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: 'Magic', debug: false },                  // names on the Controls screen; false hides one\n44\t295:- `hand()` and `tip()` give world points for spawning bullets or sparks; `worldOffset(p)` gives where any point in the rig's own frame (a joint in `J`) sits from its feet. `debug(r)` draws the skeleton.\n45\t316:- Input: the game's own input moves the focus (keys, d-pad, stick: up / down / left / right, a slider or a choice turns left and right), confirm presses, cancel goes back, pause closes the menu; touch taps. While a screen is open the game's actions are held back, so a menu press doesn't also att\n46\t343:- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return { scene, hero, score } }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }`: your game's handle. Tests read it; `tools/check.mjs` prints it after play; `tools/replay.mjs` logs it at the end of a replay.\n47\t352:game.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0); I.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);   // facing the roof's wall: jump takes hold of it\n48\t354:if (game.debug.snapshot().hero[2] !== 32) throw new Error('the hero should have climbed onto the roof');\n49\t364:- **The modules:** `grid` (square and hex grids: A* paths, move ranges with climb and drop past allies, lines, symmetric fields of view, `E.Fog`, flood fills and groups, tactics' shapes of effect, facing and threat maps, `E.GridMover` for Pac-Man's and Sokoban's moves, `E.Turns` by speed, charge\n50\t384:  - `--log \"My3D2dge.current.sceneName\"` prints any state at the end (a game's `game.debug.snapshot()` prints by itself);\n51\t452:- `new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [10000] })` keeps the score, lives, two players' turns (each one's stage in `p.save`), the continue, the tables with initials and the attract mode; `cab.update(dt)` each step and `cab.draw(r, box)` after the game.\n52\t627:  - An autopilot drives the hero through a virtual input for balance runs and an attract-mode demo.\n53\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eca6c66-8849-4edb-a442-cc89add0a71e","uuid":"b8451453-6cd6-428c-b8fd-4a64e6da5a3c","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:40.785Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/cc-plan-x4394d1/out/guide-h.txt","content":"1:# my-3D2dge guide for AI models\n7:## North star\n17:## The mental model\n29:## Remake workflow (port, remaster, reimagine, remix)\n44:## Visual craft: aim for PS1 / N64 era 2D, not NES\n64:## Animation: fluid, varied, readable\n72:## Hard rules\n82:## Standard features (built in: adjust them, don't rebuild them)\n120:## Frame order\n140:## Systems in more depth\n142:### Views and resolution\n150:### Scenes\n155:### Camera\n163:### Players (two to four on one machine)\n169:### Motion and timing (tweens, scripts, paths)\n178:### TileMap (ground-plane levels)\n190:### Heights: roofs, ledges, sight and reach\n222:### PlatformMap (side-scrolling levels)\n242:### Platformer (side-scroller controller)\n249:### Body (ground-plane physics)\n255:### Mover and actions (third-person ground controller)\n267:### Perception (sight, hearing, suspicion)\n273:### Attack (melee timing)\n280:### Bullets and patterns\n286:### Humanoid\n297:### Audio\n305:### Text and UI\n311:### Shell (an HTML interface: screens and HUD)\n319:### Lighting\n328:### Errors and warnings\n338:### Testing without a browser\n357:### The handoff package\n360:### Modules (general systems in files of their own)\n367:### Kits and the diet (which file for which game)\n374:### Recorded sessions (a bug from a phone, replayed exactly)\n402:## Genre recipes\n606:## Building a big game: lessons from Emberdeep\n631:## Where to find more: animation and examples\n648:## Performance\n656:## Checklist before handing a game back\n===\n41:6. **Tune the feel** with the feel numbers in `API.md`, then check the game with the skeleton overlay (`rig.debug(r)`) and in slow motion (`game.timeScale = .25`).\n101:    controls: { attack: 'Sword', skill: 'Magic', debug: false },                  // names on the Controls screen; false hides one\n295:- `hand()` and `tip()` give world points for spawning bullets or sparks; `worldOffset(p)` gives where any point in the rig's own frame (a joint in `J`) sits from its feet. `debug(r)` draws the skeleton.\n316:- Input: the game's own input moves the focus (keys, d-pad, stick: up / down / left / right, a slider or a choice turns left and right), confirm presses, cancel goes back, pause closes the menu; touch taps. While a screen is open the game's actions are held back, so a menu press doesn't also att\n343:- `game.debug = { snapshot() { return { scene, hero, score } }, teleport(x, y, z) {...} }`: your game's handle. Tests read it; `tools/check.mjs` prints it after play; `tools/replay.mjs` logs it at the end of a replay.\n352:game.debug.teleport(100, 88, 0, 0); I.tap('jump'); game.advance(.1);   // facing the roof's wall: jump takes hold of it\n354:if (game.debug.snapshot().hero[2] !== 32) throw new Error('the hero should have climbed onto the roof');\n364:- **The modules:** `grid` (square and hex grids: A* paths, move ranges with climb and drop past allies, lines, symmetric fields of view, `E.Fog`, flood fills and groups, tactics' shapes of effect, facing and threat maps, `E.GridMover` for Pac-Man's and Sokoban's moves, `E.Turns` by speed, charge\n384:  - `--log \"My3D2dge.current.sceneName\"` prints any state at the end (a game's `game.debug.snapshot()` prints by itself);\n452:- `new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [10000] })` keeps the score, lives, two players' turns (each one's stage in `p.save`), the continue, the tables with initials and the attract mode; `cab.update(dt)` each step and `cab.draw(r, box)` after the game.\n627:  - An autopilot drives the hero through a virtual input for balance runs and an attract-mode demo.\n","numLines":53,"startLine":1,"totalLines":53}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_017uxjjKQLBkTaFFQB5uN6FH","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
