{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01CZ5ZoyvA7xULPL7pbxYTwd","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t47:**Why games look cheap, and the fix for each:**\n2\t57:**Art recipes by classic** (combine with the genre recipes below):\n3\t405:**Side-scroller (Mario, Mega Man, Castlevania).**\n4\t421:**Metroidvania (Metroid, Super Metroid, Symphony of the Night).** Start from the METROIDVANIA slice (the rooms module).\n5\t427:**Zelda-like adventure.**\n6\t432:**Beat-'em-up (Final Fight, Streets of Rage).** Start from the BRAWLER slice.\n7\t438:**Fighting game (Street Fighter II, Darkstalkers).** Start from the FIGHTING slice (the fight module).\n8\t443:**Shoot-'em-up (1942, Gradius).** Start from the SHOOTER slice: its first stage is vertical, its second horizontal.\n9\t450:**Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids).** Start from the ARCADE slice: a cabinet of three.\n10\t456:**Kart racing (Super Mario Kart, F-Zero).** Start from the KART slice (the mode7 and drive modules).\n11\t461:**Road racing (OutRun, Pole Position, Hang-On).** Start from the ROAD slice (the road module).\n12\t465:**Top-down racing and driving (Micro Machines, RC Pro-Am, GTA).** `E.Car` on a TileMap in the `topdown` view: the same cars, laps and drivers as the kart (`\n13\t467:**JRPG (Dragon Quest, Final Fantasy).** Start from the RPG slice (the story and rpg modules).\n14\t474:**Puzzle (Tetris, Dr. Mario, Puyo Puyo).** Start from the PUZZLE slice.\n15\t480:**Roguelike (Rogue, Mystery Dungeon, Shiren).** Start from the ROGUELIKE slice.\n16\t485:**Tactics (Final Fantasy Tactics, Tactics Ogre, Fire Emblem).** Start from the TACTICS slice (the grid and story modules).\n17\t493:**Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword).** Start from the POINT-AND-CLICK slice (the click and story modules). The cl\n18\t498:**Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad).** A painted backdrop per scene (`r.overlay`), the speaker's rig large (`rig.dra