ory modules).\n493:**Point-and-click adventure (Monkey Island, Day of the Tentacle, Broken Sword).** Start from the POINT-AND-CLICK slice (the click and story modules). The cl\n498:**Visual novel (Phoenix Wright, Snatcher, Clannad).** A painted backdrop per scene (`r.overlay`), the speaker's rig large (`rig.drawPortrait(g, x, y, 120, {\n500:**Real-time strategy (Dune II, Warcraft II, Command & Conquer, StarCraft).** Start from the RTS slice (the grid and strategy modules). The strategy module (\n506:**Theme park or city sim (Theme Park, RollerCoaster Tycoon, SimCity).** Start from the SIM slice (the grid and strategy modules).\n512:**3D-era remake (Mario 64, Ocarina, Crash).**\n516:**Third-person stealth and parkour (Assassin's Creed, Metal Gear, Tenchu).** Start from the STEALTH slice.\n535:**Physics toys (Breakout, Asteroids with real collisions, Lemmings).** The physics and terrain modules; each step `world.step(dt)` from the game's fixed ste\n541:**Pinball (Pinball Fantasies, Space Cadet).** The PINBALL kit. A view of its own looking steeply down the table (`new E.View('pinball', 'Table', 0, 62, 1, 1\n548:**Artillery (Worms, Scorched Earth).** The ARTILLERY kit. A side view at a whole scale, so the terrain's cells stay square: `new E.View('artillery', 'Island\n555:**Rhythm (Dance Dance Revolution, PaRappa, Beatmania).** The RHYTHM kit. The songs module's songs and the rhythm module's `E.Rhythm`.\n562:**Survival horror (Resident Evil, Alone in the Dark).** The 3D HORROR kit. Each room its own fixed camera (`world.camera.zones`, mode `'zones'`: fixed, turn\n564:**3D kart racing (Mario Kart 64, Crash Team Racing).** The 3D RACING kit (the drive module). The circuit is a `world.track` along a closed `E.Path` with hei\n566:**Rail shooter (Star Fox 64, Panzer Dragoon).** The 3D FLIGHT kit. The ship is a `world.flyer({ rail: { path, speed, w, h } })`: the rail's point rides on a\n568:**Sports (Sensible Soccer, NBA Jam, Tecmo Bowl).** Start from the SPORTS slice: two against two in a walled cage, up to four players.\n573:**First-person dungeon (Wizardry, Dungeon Master, Eye of the Beholder).** The 3D CRAWLER kit (the grid module). The 3D engine's `'fixed'` camera at the part\n575:**Twin-stick shooter (Robotron 2084, Smash TV).** Start from the ADVENTURE kit (a `Body` hero in rooms) with the SHOOTER's ships and bullets.\n579:**Bomberman.** Start from the PUZZLE slice's grid or the ARCADE's maze (the grid module).\n584:**Gauntlet.** Start from the ADVENTURE slice (a `TileMap` dungeon in `threequarter` or `topdown`).\n588:**Frogger.** An `E.Grid` of lanes in `overhead`: the frog an `E.GridMover` that hops a cell per press; each lane a row of cars or logs moving at its own spe\n590:**Sokoban.** An `E.Grid` from text rows (`#` walls, `$` crates, `.` goals, `@` you); you an `E.GridMover` with `push(cx, cy, dx, dy)` that moves a crate whe\n592:**Sonic without the loops (Sonic the Hedgehog's speed on flat ground and slopes).** Start from the PLATFORMER slice: `new E.Platformer({ momentum: true })` \n594:**Cinematic platformer (Prince of Persia, Flashback, Another World).** Start from the PLATFORMER slice with `new E.Platformer({ ledge: true, crouch: true })\n596:**Light guns (Time Crisis, The House of the Dead, Virtua Cop).** Start from the 3D FLIGHT slice's rails (or a 2D screen of `overhead` sprites): the camera r\n598:**Indoor corridor shooter (Doom, GoldenEye 007) on the 3D engine.** Start from the 3D SHOOTER slice's first person: its gun, hitscan (`world.ray`), recoil a\n600:**Mash-ups.** The kits don't depend on each other. Some examples:\n634:**Motion clips** (`docs/MOCAP.md`): 325 curated clips and all 2,548 takes of the CMU motion capture database, in a readable text format of key poses (whole \n640:**Objects and materials** (`docs/ASSETS.md`, full engine): still objects written as a few lines of named parts (a barrel is a turned profile of oak and two \n642:**Worked examples** (`src/emberdeep/`, `src/emberdeep/DESIGN.md`): Emberdeep registers every part on one line, so one search lists them all: `grep -nE \"def\\\n644:**Starters**: `dist/kits/my-3d2dge-<genre>.html`, one vertical slice per genre (21 of them: the README's kits list, the API card's playbook), each a complet\n646:**Real 3D**: `dist/my-3d2dge-3d.js` puts a three.js and Rapier world under a game (make the game with `bg: null`); its header is its manual, with a complete\n","numLines":47,"startLine":1,"totalLines":47}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01CZ5ZoyvA7xULPL7pbxYTwd","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggyGSYq4TJh7Z3NjaxV7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BKL4YJtQ7HibbFphQA9rbK","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.cache/cc-plan-x4394d1/engine/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md","offset":450,"limit":6},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3052,"cache_read_input_tokens":127969,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3052},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eca6c66-8849-4edb-a442-cc89add0a71e","uuid":"8108d7f7-a1a6-4ac6-a6de-07cd8b1c69f3","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:59.268Z","request_id":"req_011CggyGSKCJRGT9NeUk9spv","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01BKL4YJtQ7HibbFphQA9rbK":{"file_path":"/home/micha/.cache/cc-plan-x4394d1/engine/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md","offset":450,"limit":6}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01BKL4YJtQ7HibbFphQA9rbK","type":"tool_result","content":"450\t**Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids).** Start from the ARCADE slice: a cabinet of three.\n451\t- One fixed screen (`res: [232, 270]` or `[320, 240]` with `expand`): centre the playfield and fill the rest with cabinet art drawn by code, or let the field be the whole screen (the rocks wrap at its edges).\n452\t- `new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [10000] })` keeps the score, lives, two players' turns (each one's stage in `p.save`), the continue, the tables with initials and the attract mode; `cab.update(dt)` each step and `cab.draw(r, box)` after the game.\n453\t- A maze is an `E.Grid` with `E.GridMover`s: the player's turn asked early is kept (`{ keep: true }`); a chaser picks, at each cell, the open way nearest its own target (never straight back). Moths fly in on `E.Path`s and turn with `r.sprite`'s `rot`; rocks drift with `E.wrap` and draw at every edge they cross.\n454\t- Each game's demo is its own bot, playing the real rules; a remaster (light, rigs, glow) with the classic look one key and one setting away.\n455\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eca6c66-8849-4edb-a442-cc89add0a71e","uuid":"6effff57-a0fc-430d-b63e-82e17c54cfbc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:50:59.276Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/cc-plan-x4394d1/engine/dist/handoff/AI_GUIDE.md","content":"**Golden-age arcade (Pac-Man, Galaga, Asteroids).** Start from the ARCADE slice: a cabinet of three.\n- One fixed screen (`res: [232, 270]` or `[320, 240]` with `expand`): centre the playfield and fill the rest with cabinet art drawn by code, or let the field be the whole screen (the rocks wrap at its edges).\n- `new E.Arcade(game, { id, lives: 3, extra: [10000] })` keeps the score, lives, two players' turns (each one's stage in `p.save`), the continue, the tables with initials and the attract mode; `cab.update(dt)` each step and `cab.draw(r, box)` after the game.\n- A maze is an `E.Grid` with `E.GridMover`s: the player's turn asked early is kept (`{ keep: true }`); a chaser picks, at each cell, the open way nearest its own target (never straight back). Moths fly in on `E.Path`s and turn with `r.sprite`'s `rot`; rocks drift with `E.wrap` and draw at every edge they cross.\n- Each game's demo is its own bot, playing the real rules; a remaster (light, rigs, glow) with the classic look one key and one setting away.\n","numLines":6,"startLine":450,"totalLines":665}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01BKL4YJtQ7HibbFphQA9rbK","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
