{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fu8MwWc3J7EW3NR2rqeKcw","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n2\t100:- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n3\t283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n4\t292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n5\t297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n6\t299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n7\t308:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n8\t311:- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n9\t326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n10\t329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n11\t341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n12\t360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n13\t426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or\n14\t483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n15\t485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n16\t545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n17\t627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n18\t761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.\n19\t851:- `level.crumble(cx, cz, holds = .5, respawn = 3)` †: start a crumbling block at a cell going, once (it falls away after holds seconds and comes back after respawn more; 0: never; update(dt) runs them, each step); returns its record\n20\t1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n21\t1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n22\t1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n23\t1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n24\t1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n25\t1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n26\t1573:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n27\t1575:- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\n28\t1605:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n29\t1695:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\n30\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eca6c66-8849-4edb-a442-cc89add0a71e","uuid":"7a2498d5-e7d8-47cf-ab02-2b74be3341bb","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:52:07.735Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/cc-plan-x4394d1/out/idx1.txt","content":"88:- 1161 21d. Shell; E.Shell: shell\n100:- 1573 Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js); E.Road: road\n283:- `input.codeLabel(code)`: a code as a person reads it: 'W' (or the keyboard's own letter there), 'Space', '↑', 'Left click', and a gamepad button by its symbol on the controller in use ('A', '✕', 'B'...; glyphs picks the family)\n292:- `input.label(a, device = this.lastDevice)`: the key or button to show in a prompt for action a, on the device the player used last (or the one named: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch'), with their bindings: input.label('jump') -> 'Space', 'A' or '✕'\n297:- `input.padStyle()`: the controller family whose symbols label() shows: glyphs, or with glyphs 'auto' the one its name says\n299:- `input.pointer()` †: the mouse pointer in screen pixels [x, y] (the HUD's space), or null before it has moved over the canvas\n308:- `input.rumble(strength = .5, seconds = .15)` †: shake the gamepad: strength 0..1 for seconds (scaled by rumbleScale; nothing where the controller can't). Returns true when it rumbled\n311:- `input.stopRumble()` †: stop a rumble now (pause, focus lost, unplugged)\n326:- `input.glyphs = 'auto'`: the gamepad's button symbols for label(): 'auto' (from the controller's name) | 'xbox' | 'playstation' | 'nintendo' | 'generic' (positions)\n329:- `input.lastDevice = 'keyboard'`: 'keyboard' | 'mouse' | 'gamepad' | 'touch', the last one used (show the right button prompts)\n341:- `input.rumbleScale = .6` †: vibration strength 0..1 (0 = off; game.settings.rumble sets it)\n360:- `E.font.title(g, s, x, y, o = {})`: Big logo text for title screens: scaled glyphs with a vertical color gradient, an outline and an extruded 3D edge. title(g, 'CASTLE OF NIGHT', x, y, { scale: 3, colors: ['#fff6c8', '#ffd36a', '#e07a2a'], outline: '#1a0c10', depth: 3, depthColor: '#6a2a1a', align: 'center' })\n426:- `r.pick(sx, sy)` †: what was drawn under a screen point (the HUD's pixels: input.clicked(), input.pointer()) in the last frame, front to back: the pick values of the actors, sprites, props and queued draws given one (r.actor(x, y, z, fn, { pick: unit })), each where its pixels went (an actor's drawn bounds; others' box, or\n483:- `game.hitFx(x, y, z, o = {})`: everything a good hit needs in one call: hit-stop, shake, an impact star, sparks along the hit direction, a sound, a damage number and a rumble on a gamepad. hitFx(x, y, z, { power: 1, angle, damage, color, sound: 'hit', rumble: true })\n485:- `game.mouseGround()`: mouse position on the ground (world units), or null\n545:- `game.shell = null` †: the E.Shell over this game (an HTML interface: screens and HUD), or null\n627:- `saves.show(mode = 'load', done)` †: open the standard save screen over the game (E.Shell's): 'save' (to a slot) or 'load'; done(save) after a load or a save. False without a menu (a headless game, menu: false)\n761:- `map.pick(sx, sy, at = E.current)`: the cell under a screen point on a map with heights (tactics, strategy, board games): the first top or wall face the line of sight meets, front to back, in any view, turn and zoom. sx, sy: the HUD's pixels (input.clicked(), input.pointer()); at: the game whose view and camera drew it (E.\n851:- `level.crumble(cx, cz, holds = .5, respawn = 3)` †: start a crumbling block at a cell going, once (it falls away after holds seconds and comes back after respawn more; 0: never; update(dt) runs them, each step); returns its record\n1163:- `new E.Shell(game, o = {}) → shell`: new E.Shell(game, { theme, screens: { name: spec }, settings: { items, onChange(settings, key) }, store: 'shell-settings', meters: .125, standard: true }): an HTML interface over the game (see the section's header)\n1164:- `new E.Shell({ theme })`: CSS variables (ink, paper, accent, muted, danger, line, font, titleFont)\n1165:- `new E.Shell({ screens })`: specs ui.show(name) starts from (the pause screen follows game.paused; screens: { pause: false } leaves it out)\n1166:- `new E.Shell({ settings })`: settings.items: the game's own settings, { key, label, type: 'toggle' | 'slider' | 'select', min, max, step, options, value } (kept in game.settings, beside the standard ones)\n1167:- `new E.Shell({ store, meters })`: store: where an older version saved them; meters: meters per world unit for distances\n1168:- `new E.Shell({ standard })`: false leaves out the standard menu (the pause screen's Settings, Controls, Full screen and Quit, and the settings' groups)\n1573:## Module road: the pseudo-3D road: segments with curves and hills, lanes, rumble strips, roadside scenery, tunnels (engine/modules/road.js)\n1575:- `new E.Road(o = {}) → road`: new E.Road({ segment, width, lanes, rumble, draw, fov, height, colors, fog, sky }): a road (the manual above)\n1605:- `world.shellMap()`: the explored map for E.Shell's minimap: game.shell.hud({ minimap: world.shellMap() }) (a cell a square, the save and boss rooms marked, the hero's cell)\n1695:- `strategy.minimap(colors = {})` †: E.Shell's minimap spec: the map, the fog, the camera's view, the units seen as dots by side, a click moving the camera\n","numLines":30,"startLine":1,"totalLines":30}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01Fu8MwWc3J7EW3NR2rqeKcw","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
