{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01DBt4V5Gi22dVcbvfoUuvk6","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n2\t1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the mus\n3\t1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n4\t1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n5\t1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n6\t1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n7\t1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n8\t===FILTER\n9\t187:- `E.targets(from, list, o = {})`: the things in list that `from` can reach, nearest first, each as { target, d (ground distance), dz, angle (from -> it) }: melee auto-aim, lock-on, takedowns, interaction prompts. o: { range, arc (half angle arou\n10\t261:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.filter sets it\n11\t===MUSIC\n12\t514:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\n13\t1050:- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n14\t1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n15\t1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n16\t1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s .\n17\t1065:- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n18\t1642:- `E.Songbook.get(id)`: a song by id (playable: game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get('town'))), or undefined\n19\t1644:- `E.Songbook.songs`: every song by id ({ title, mood: [...], bpm, steps, tracks, loop }; the core's own songs are E.songs')\n20\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eca6c66-8849-4edb-a442-cc89add0a71e","uuid":"d384cc50-d236-4ba1-98b7-8e4f61cc20cc","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:56:54.354Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/cc-plan-x4394d1/out/audio1.txt","content":"1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1063:- `game.audio.sfx(what, o = {})`: Play a sound effect: a preset name ('jump', 'coin', 'hit', 'explode', ...), a voice object, or a list of voices. opts: { vol: 0..1, pitch: multiplier, vary: random pitch spread (default 0.03), step: a step of the music playing (it sounds on that step of the mus\n1075:- `game.audio.presets`: the named sound effects, sfx(name) plays one and define(name, voice) adds one\n1106:- `new E.Dialog(game, o = {}) → talk`: new E.Dialog(game, { speed, lines, place, color, nameColor, voice, bg, border, vars }): a dialog box that types its text; say() opens it, update(dt) and draw(r) run it\n1134:- `talk.voice = 'text'`: the sound effect each letter blips ('text'; null for silence)\n1543:- `new E.Rhythm(game, o = {}) → rhythm` †: new E.Rhythm(game, { song, chart, lanes, windows, life, lead, voice, on }): see the manual\n1570:- `rhythm.voice` †: the calls' sound\n===FILTER\n187:- `E.targets(from, list, o = {})`: the things in list that `from` can reach, nearest first, each as { target, d (ground distance), dz, angle (from -> it) }: melee auto-aim, lock-on, takedowns, interaction prompts. o: { range, arc (half angle arou\n261:- `game.screen.filter = 'clean'` †: 'clean' | 'scanlines' | 'crt', drawn over the picture as it is presented, never on the buffer, and not under a test harness (navigator.webdriver). game.settings.filter sets it\n===MUSIC\n514:- `game.audio`: chip-sound synthesizer: game.audio.sfx('jump'), game.audio.music(song)\n1050:- `E.songs: title, adventure, dungeon, boss, victory`: ready-made chiptune loops (original compositions). game.audio.music('adventure')\n1054:- `game.audio.define(name, voice)`: add or replace a named sound: audio.define('zap', { wave: 'saw', freq: 1200, to: 200, dur: .2 })\n1056:- `game.audio.layer(track, vol = 1, fade = .5)` †: a track's volume as the song plays, 0..1, faded over fade seconds: layers of one song (the chase's drums in when the guards see you, out when they lose you). track: its index in song.tracks, or its name\n1057:- `game.audio.music(song, o = {})`: Loop a song (or play once with { loop: false }). song = { bpm: 120, steps: 4, tracks: [ { wave: 'square', vol: .2, notes: 'C5 - E5 - G5 - . . | ...' }, one token per step { wave: 'triangle', notes: 'C3 . C3 . G2 . G2 .' }, { wave: 'drums', notes: 'k . h . s .\n1065:- `game.audio.stopMusic(fade)`: stop the music (it fades out over fade seconds, .06 by default)\n1642:- `E.Songbook.get(id)`: a song by id (playable: game.audio.music(E.Songbook.get('town'))), or undefined\n1644:- `E.Songbook.songs`: every song by id ({ title, mood: [...], bpm, steps, tracks, loop }; the core's own songs are E.songs')\n","numLines":20,"startLine":1,"totalLines":20}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01DBt4V5Gi22dVcbvfoUuvk6","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
