{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01T9NtQCRE5uMfuRWBa2oYy7","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Objects and materials as data\n2\t\n3\tThe full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\n4\twith the house shading and outline, and gives every surface (floors, wall faces, wall tops, platform tiles, the objects'\n5\town faces) a material from one open registry. An object costs one to a few hundred tokens of data (the core's median is\n6\t125); you check it headless with one command. Read this card whole before you write one. (The agent edition keeps the\n7\tregistries and ignores the calls: `E.addAssets` returns empty lists, the others null.)\n8\t\n9\t## Use one\n10\t\n11\t```js\n12\t// in draw(r): feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor; its front toward facing\n13\tr.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n14\t// once, before the updates: bodies stop at it, a body coming down lands on it, one wholly below passes under\n15\tmap.solid('table', 120, 80, 0, { facing: 0 });\n16\t// a sprite of it, for an inventory or a HUD (r.sprite, px.sprite)\n17\tconst icon = E.shapeSprite('chest', { view: 'iso' });\n18\t```\n19\t\n20\t- **r.shape options:** facing (radians, where the front points: 0 east, π/2 south, as written), scale, mats ({ slot:\n21\t  material }), flip (mirrors it x to -x, collision too), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (default true),\n22\t  light (adds its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true).\n23\t- **map.solid** takes the same id and placement, so one object can feed both calls. Bodies span z to z + h (E.Body's h, 32).\n24\t- **In 3D** the 3D engine draws the same entries, materials and boxes: `world.shape(id, x, y, z, o)` (its header).\n25\t- **Steep views** (top-down) draw shapes from the characters' lower angle, as rigs are drawn. The light comes from the\n26\t  viewer's upper left in every view.\n27\t- **Glow and fire:** a material with glow: 1 ignores the light and stays bright in the dark; an entry's flames ([[x, y, z,\n28\t  w, h]]) draw the engine's animated flame (r.shape only: a sprite has none). Anything else that moves stays a prop\n29\t  (r.prop) or your own code.\n30\t- **Dressing a generated level:** a scene is a few entries as [id, across, forward] from an anchor (a wall spot, forward\n31\t  into the room); place it whole or not at all, each part on free floor, after the level's own random picks and from a\n32\t  seeded stream of its own, so the level stays as its seed builds it (Emberdeep's `src/emberdeep/53-scenes.js`).\n33\t\n34\t## The core library\n35\t\n36\t**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\n37\tbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\n38\ttree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n39\t`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n40\t\n41\t**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\n42\tbrick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\n43\tplants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\n44\twalls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n45\t\n46\t## Materials on surfaces\n47\t\n48\t```js\n49\tE.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\n50\tconst types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\n51\tconst map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\n52\tconst level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n53\t```\n54\t\n55\tfloorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n56\t\n57\tA material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n58\t(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\n59\tevery surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\n60\tOverlays, the last on top, each in its own color's tones: `over: [['moss', '#5f7a3a', { up: .6 }], ['cracks']]`; moss on\n61\twhat looks up, cracks (the material a step darker), dirt near the ground (h 6), rust; each takes amount and size.\n62\t\n63\t| Pattern | Numbers | What |\n64\t| --- | --- | --- |\n65\t| none | | the light alone |\n66\t| planks | bw 3, len 14, dir | boards with joints; staves on round parts; dir: 'v' turns them |\n67\t| crate | frame 2, bw 3 | a framed, braced side; planks on its lid |\n68\t| bricks | bw 6, bh 3, mortar | running bond |\n69\t| stones | size 5 | irregular stones (Voronoi), dark joints, a lit rim |\n70\t| tiles | size 4 | square tiles, grout |"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eca6c66-8849-4edb-a442-cc89add0a71e","uuid":"42ea22de-3c5a-4a62-abd3-99bf326738f5","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:57:49.063Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/.cache/cc-plan-x4394d1/engine/dist/handoff/docs/ASSETS.md","content":"# Objects and materials as data\n\nThe full engine draws still objects (barrels, tables, trees, wells) from a few lines of data, in every view and facing,\nwith the house shading and outline, and gives every surface (floors, wall faces, wall tops, platform tiles, the objects'\nown faces) a material from one open registry. An object costs one to a few hundred tokens of data (the core's median is\n125); you check it headless with one command. Read this card whole before you write one. (The agent edition keeps the\nregistries and ignores the calls: `E.addAssets` returns empty lists, the others null.)\n\n## Use one\n\n```js\n// in draw(r): feet on the point, depth sorted like an actor; its front toward facing\nr.shape('barrel', x, y, 0, { facing: Math.PI / 2 });\n// once, before the updates: bodies stop at it, a body coming down lands on it, one wholly below passes under\nmap.solid('table', 120, 80, 0, { facing: 0 });\n// a sprite of it, for an inventory or a HUD (r.sprite, px.sprite)\nconst icon = E.shapeSprite('chest', { view: 'iso' });\n```\n\n- **r.shape options:** facing (radians, where the front points: 0 east, π/2 south, as written), scale, mats ({ slot:\n  material }), flip (mirrors it x to -x, collision too), params (a generator's: { h: 30 }), bias, hides (default true),\n  light (adds its lights to game.lights), shadow (default true).\n- **map.solid** takes the same id and placement, so one object can feed both calls. Bodies span z to z + h (E.Body's h, 32).\n- **In 3D** the 3D engine draws the same entries, materials and boxes: `world.shape(id, x, y, z, o)` (its header).\n- **Steep views** (top-down) draw shapes from the characters' lower angle, as rigs are drawn. The light comes from the\n  viewer's upper left in every view.\n- **Glow and fire:** a material with glow: 1 ignores the light and stays bright in the dark; an entry's flames ([[x, y, z,\n  w, h]]) draw the engine's animated flame (r.shape only: a sprite has none). Anything else that moves stays a prop\n  (r.prop) or your own code.\n- **Dressing a generated level:** a scene is a few entries as [id, across, forward] from an anchor (a wall spot, forward\n  into the room); place it whole or not at all, each part on free floor, after the level's own random picks and from a\n  seeded stream of its own, so the level stays as its seed builds it (Emberdeep's `src/emberdeep/53-scenes.js`).\n\n## The core library\n\n**Shapes** (sized for a 26-unit hero; generators take params): barrel, crate, chest, table, chair, stool, bench, bed,\nbookcase, shelf, pot, jar, sack, cart, well, sign, lamppost, anvil; fence { len: 16 }, pine { h: 41, tiers: 4 },\ntree { h: 40, seed: 1 }, bush { r: 7 }, grass { h: 6, n: 6 }, rock { r: 7.5, seed: 2 }, crystal { h: 18, seed: 1 }.\n`r.shape('pine', x, y, 0, { params: { h: 30 } })`; `E.SHAPES.barrel.about` says what each is.\n\n**Materials:** woods oak walnut birch crate plank planks wood; stones stone cobble marble granite sandstone slate rock\nbrick flagstone ruin; metals iron steel gold copper bronze metal rusted; clay glazed porcelain; cloth linen burlap wool velvet leather;\nplants bark needles leaves shrub moss straw hedge grass; ground dirt sand snow mud; water ice crystal flame bone shingle;\nwalls timber plaster; tops speckle plain tiles slab; tiles block bonus ground pipe checker.\n\n## Materials on surfaces\n\n```js\nE.MATERIALS.mossy = { color: '#6a7a5a', pattern: 'stones', size: 6 };   // or the shorthand '#6a7a5a stones size=6'\nconst types = { 1: { h: 32, top: '#6a6280', side: '#4a4360', face: 'cobble', roof: 'slate' } };   // TileMap walls\nconst map = new E.TileMap({ rows, legend, types, floorMat: 'flagstone', floorMats: { water: 'water' } });   // floors\nconst level = new E.PlatformMap({ rows, legend, types: { 1: { kind: 'solid', style: 'block', mat: 'mossy' } } });\n```\n\nfloorMats is keyed by the floor tags of the legend ('~': { floor: 'water' }); either stands in for floorTex.\n\nA material is `{ color, pattern, ...the pattern's numbers, ramp, glow, over }`. Its five tones come from `E.tones(color)`\n(or its own `ramp` of five, dark to light); the light picks a band, the pattern moves it a step, so a material works on\nevery surface and in every palette and recolors with one hex. An unknown name warns with the list of names.\nOverlays, the last on top, each in its own color's tones: `over: [['moss', '#5f7a3a', { up: .6 }], ['cracks']]`; moss on\nwhat looks up, cracks (the material a step darker), dirt near the ground (h 6), rust; each takes amount and size.\n\n| Pattern | Numbers | What |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| none | | the light alone |\n| planks | bw 3, len 14, dir | boards with joints; staves on round parts; dir: 'v' turns them |\n| crate | frame 2, bw 3 | a framed, braced side; planks on its lid |\n| bricks | bw 6, bh 3, mortar | running bond |\n| stones | size 5 | irregular stones (Voronoi), dark joints, a lit rim |\n| tiles | size 4 | square tiles, grout |","numLines":70,"startLine":1,"totalLines":161}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01T9NtQCRE5uMfuRWBa2oYy7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
