shC, .9, 0, -.8), n1 = Sp(J.hipC, 1.1, 0, 1.4); px.line(g, n0[0], n0[1], n1[0], n1[1], t.sh); const c0 = Sp(J.shC, .7, -.9, -.2), c1 = Sp(J.shC, 1.1, 0, -1.3), c2 = Sp(J.shC, .7, .9, -.2\n===IDX\n165:- `E.ik3(a, b, L1, L2, hint)`: two-bone IK in 3D: returns [joint, end]. hint points the way the joint should bend.\n675:- `rig.solvePose()`: set the joints J from the rig's state this step (update and setPose call it); a clip player may wrap it on one rig: const base = rig.solvePose; rig.solvePose = function () { base.call(this); ...move J... }\n677:- `rig.update(dt, s = {})`: s: { x, y, z, vx, vy, facing, dash, hurt, attack, air, point } air: true while jumping or falling (legs tuck), point: true to hold the weapon hand forward (aiming a gun) attack: { spec, phase: 'wind' | 'active' | 'recover', u: 0..1 }. spec.kick = true swings the right foot instead of the hand also\n678:- `rig.worldOffset(p)`: where a point in the rig's own frame ([forward, right, up]; a joint such as rig.J.head, or one offset from it) sits, in world units from the rig's feet: add rig.x, y, z for the world point, or project it to draw at a joint\n680:- `rig.J`: its joints this step in its own frame ({ hipL, kneeL, footL, shC, head, handR, ... }; rig.worldOffset(J.handR) gives one in the world)\n697:- `rig.spin = 0`: the body's extra turn during a spinning move, radians\n","numLines":48,"startLine":1,"totalLines":48}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01L6izyoEKcLjJCnTNxW12MV","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
