{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cgh2RxG7SDdfhZRJvFxh7","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NA1xtZFoz4zj527Ae1YXgB","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174834__x4394d1/work/PLAN.md","offset":1625,"limit":170},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":9305,"cache_read_input_tokens":517119,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":9305},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eca6c66-8849-4edb-a442-cc89add0a71e","uuid":"6126aaa2-2a18-4bc1-bc96-331ece66faa0","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:32:30.767Z","request_id":"req_011Cgh2RwzjfLnxHEKyJ4Vjz","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_01NA1xtZFoz4zj527Ae1YXgB":{"file_path":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174834__x4394d1/work/PLAN.md","offset":1625,"limit":170}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NA1xtZFoz4zj527Ae1YXgB","type":"tool_result","content":"1625\t- **The tabloid page, the travel map, the bracket cards, the sticker frames:** UI art in code.\n1626\t- **Weather and pyro overlays:** fog layers, flare smoke, confetti, fireworks (particles).\n1627\t\n1628\tFrom the engine's library (generic props, `node tools/asset-find.mjs`): benches (`bench`, `kenney-holiday:bench`) for\n1629\tthe dugouts and the training ground; `lamppost` and `kenney-graveyard:lightpost-double` on the harbour road; `fence`\n1630\tand `kenney-fantasy-town:hedge` at the rec ground; `kenney-holiday:snowman` outside the Stahlpresse Arena;\n1631\t`kenney-fantasy-town:stall-red` market stalls (the pie stand, the Kipperton harbour); `kenney-pirate:flag` on the\n1632\ttrawler; palms (`r.prop('palm')`) at Solera; `crate`, `barrel` and `sign` at the harbour. Load an asset set with its\n1633\tscript before `game.js` and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-holiday'])`, or cut the few entries the game uses into\n1634\ta set of its own with `tools/asset-set.mjs`.\n1635\t\n1636\t### 8.3 Animation\n1637\t\n1638\tThree sources, all on the engine's Humanoid rig: (a) the engine's own animation (gait from velocity, `E.MOVES`-style\n1639\tattack specs, poses, expressions); (b) mocap clips through `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` (set `rig.mocap` each step,\n1640\t`rig.mocapW` to fade, `rig.mocapMask = 'upper'` for the arms over the legs); (c) procedural recipes: the tilt state\n1641\t(§5.3) and joint post-processing (wrap `rig.solvePose`, as the API card shows).\n1642\t\n1643\t**Cut the clip set** (run in the scratch clone of the engine repository):\n1644\t\n1645\t```sh\n1646\tnode tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js \\\n1647\t  examples/cmu-lib/CMU_10.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_11.js \\\n1648\t  --clips \"QUATERNIUS:Slide_Start,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Exit,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Knockback,QUATERNIUS:LayToIdle,QUATERNIUS:OverhandThrow,QUATERNIUS:Roll,Victory,Cheer_One_arm,Cheering_Two_Hands,Dance_Simple,Angry,Backflip,Help_Two_Arms,Death_C,Dodge_left,Dodge_right,Greeting,Cartwheel,Jump_Twist,Breakdance_Helicopter,Shrug,Fall_On_Face,Get_Up_Face_Down,Get_Up_From_Back,Get_Up_From_Side,Run_Quick_Stop,Wave_Hello,10_02,10_05,11_01\" \\\n1649\t  --name EF --title \"Europhoria Football\" --out <dev folder>/mocap/ef-clips.js \\\n1650\t  --credit \"Quaternius Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 (CC0); Mesh2Motion (CC0); CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (mocap.cs.cmu.edu), free for all uses; created with funding from NSF EIA-0196217.\"\n1651\t```\n1652\t\n1653\tIf a name is in more than one set, the tool says so: prefix it `SET:`. If a clip's name differs, check the set's\n1654\tcatalog (`src/mocap/catalogs/*.json`) and fix the list. Expect about 150–250 KB. The CMU soccer takes play only a\n1655\twindow around the kick: find the contact time once (the frame where the right foot's forward reach peaks), store it in\n1656\t`EF.Anim.CLIPS`, and sample from `contact − 0.45 s` to `contact + 0.35 s`.\n1657\t\n1658\t| Moment | Source | How |\n1659\t|---|---|---|\n1660\t| idle, jog, run, sprint | engine | the gait from velocity; `sprint: true` adds the lean |\n1661\t| dribble touch | engine spec | `touch: { rel, kick: true, a0: .2, a1: 0, z0: .08, z1: .12, reach: 4, wind: .03, active: .04, recover: .08 }` every stride |\n1662\t| pass | engine spec | `pass: { rel, kick: true, a0: .6, a1: -.1, z0: .15, z1: .2, reach: 6, wind: .08, active: .08, recover: .16, twist: .4 }` (inside foot) |\n1663\t| shot | spec, plus mocap for power ≥ .8 | `shot: { rel, kick: true, a0: .05, a1: 0, z0: .3, z1: 1.1, reach: 7, wind: .12, active: .1, recover: .26, lean: -.25, lunge: 2 }`; at high power blend `10_02`'s kick window in over the spec (`mocapW` 1, then fading to 0 in the recovery) |\n1664\t| penalty run-up and kick | mocap | `11_01` (the run-up and kick), with root motion supplied by the body |\n1665\t| chip / lob | spec | `chip: { a0: .1, a1: 0, z0: .1, z1: 1.4, reach: 5.5, lean: -.4 }` |\n1666\t| volley | spec | `volley: { a0: .4, a1: -.2, z0: .9, z1: 1.2, reach: 7, hop: 2, lean: -.4, twist: .6 }` |\n1667\t| header | procedural | `air: true` with a z arc; tilt forward 20° (axis `right`); the head snaps forward at contact (post-process `J.head`) |\n1668\t| diving header | procedural | tilt +75° about `right` (pivot hips, lift 6), arms back; lands with `down` 0.5 s; up with `Get_Up_Face_Down` |\n1669\t| bicycle kick | procedural | tilt −140° about `right` (pivot hips, lift up to 14 at contact), with `axekick`-style kick: `{ kick: true, a0: .1, a1: 0, z0: 2.2, z1: 1.5, reach: 6 }`; lands on the back (`down`); up with `Get_Up_From_Back` |\n1670\t| slide tackle | mocap | `Slide_Start` → `Slide_Loop` → `Slide_Exit` (the body supplies the travel) |\n1671\t| poke tackle | spec | `poke: { kick: true, a0: .3, a1: 0, z0: .1, z1: .1, reach: 7.5, lunge: 3, wind: .05, active: .08, recover: .15 }` |\n1672\t| barge | engine move | `bash`, with a lean |\n1673\t| launched by a slide | procedural | tilt about `forward` spinning 1.5 turns over 0.6 s while the body flies (vz 120), stars; then `down: 1`; up with `LayToIdle` or `Get_Up_From_Side` |\n1674\t| knocked back | mocap | `Hit_Knockback`, then `LayToIdle` |\n1675\t| wrong-footed | mocap | `Dodge_left` / `Dodge_right` at `mocapW` .7, with `hurt` |\n1676\t| step-over | spec | two quick `kick` specs sweeping across the ball (`a0` from ±.9 to ∓.3), 0.15 s apart |\n1677\t| spin turn | engine | `rig.spin` from 0 to 2π over 0.45 s |\n1678\t| rainbow flick | spec | heel flick: `{ kick: true, a0: 3.0, a1: 2.6, z0: .1, z1: 1.3, reach: 4 }` (behind, upward) |\n1679\t| skid stop | mocap | `Run_Quick_Stop` (upper body, `mocapMask: 'upper'`) on hard stops |\n1680\t| theatrical dive | procedural + mocap | launch forward (tilt +80° about `right`, lift 8), land, 2 sideways rolls (tilt about `forward` spinning 2 turns while sliding 30), lie clutching a shin (`down: 1`, `expr: 'wince'`, hands to `J.kneeR`); if booked, up with `Shrug` |\n1681\t| protests | mocap | `Angry`, `Help_Two_Arms`, `Shrug` (upper) |\n1682\t| tired | procedural | lean 30°, hands to the knees (post-process `J.handL`/`J.handR` toward `J.kneeL`/`J.kneeR`) at stoppages when stamina is under 25 |\n1683\t| keeper set | engine | `pose: 'guard'`, crouch .3 |\n1684\t| keeper dive | procedural | tilt ±(70–95)° about `forward` (pivot feet), lifted 2 (low) to 14 (high) on an arc; lateral speed 260 easing to 0; hands IK'd (`E.ik3`) to the ball's point; then `down` on the side; up with `Get_Up_From_Side` |\n1685\t| keeper catch / parry / tip | procedural / engine | hands to the chest (catch); `jab` toward the ball (parry); one arm up with a jump (tip) |\n1686\t| keeper throw | mocap | `OverhandThrow`; an underarm roll as a spec with the arm low |\n1687\t| smother | procedural | a low forward dive (tilt +80° about `right`, lift 2) |\n1688\t| celebrations | mocap + procedural | knee slide: `Slide_Loop` with arms out (post-process); `Backflip`; `Cartwheel`; aeroplane: run with the arms horizontal (post-process) and a lean into the turn; robot: `Dance_Simple` at 0.6× speed with the arms bent square (post-process); shirt over head: `hood: true` with the hood in the shirt colour plus `Cheering_Two_Hands`; corner-flag dance: `Dance_Simple`; badge kiss: `Greeting`; helicopter: `Breakdance_Helicopter`; fish slap: two players face each other, alternating `jab` with a kipper sprite in the hand; pile-on: teammates `Victory` / `Cheer_One_arm` |\n1689\t| referee | engine + procedural | whistle (hand to mouth), points to the spot (`point: true`), the card raised high (hand above the head; the card sprite at `rig.hand('R')`), advantage (both arms forward), the VAR rectangle (both hands trace a box), hand to the ear; knocked over by the ball (`Fall_On_Face`, then up) |\n1690\t| manager | mocap | pacing (gait), `Angry` (conceding), `Victory` (scoring), `Help_Two_Arms` (instructions), `Cheering_Two_Hands` |\n1691\t| tunnel and handshakes | engine + procedural | a walk; an arm forward (`point: true`) as the lines pass |\n1692\t| crowd front rows | engine | classic-style rigs with `pose: 'cheer'`, `wave`, arms down for boos |\n1693\t\n1694\tCheck every attack and every procedural move with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (§11.7): a wind-up, a strike, and a settle\n1695\twithout jerks or backward sweeps.\n1696\t\n1697\t---\n1698\t\n1699\t## 9. Build order and milestones\n1700\t\n1701\tEach milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tools/test.mjs`), the build working, and a short note in the dev\n1702\tfolder's `PROGRESS.md`. Do them in order: each one builds on the last, and the risky parts come early.\n1703\t\n1704\t**M0 — Setup (½ day).** The dev folder; the engine copied; `vendor/` filled; `package.json`; `tools/build.mjs`\n1705\tproducing `build/game.js`, the dev page and the deliverable; `tools/test.mjs` with its vm loader and one smoke test;\n1706\t`kits/sports.js` running as `src/` fragments, unchanged, through the pipeline (proof: its `run(600)` hash is the same\n1707\ttwice).\n1708\t*Done when:* `node tools/build.mjs && node tools/test.mjs` passes, and `node tools/check.mjs` on the deliverable shows\n1709\tthe kit's cage match.\n1710\t\n1711\t**M1 — The football sandbox (the feel).** The broadcast view; the pitch geometry and TileMap (§6.1); the ball (§6.2);\n1712\t5-a-side footballers with movement, stamina and dribbling (§6.3); pass, through, lob, one-two (§6.4); shooting with\n1713\tthe meter, sweet spot, aim, curl and chip (§6.5, without air moves); possession; goals; kickoffs; a temporary formation\n1714\tAI (the kit's, widened to 5); the camera director (§6.14); the score bug and power meter; `EF.T` with the TUNE tab only\n1715\t(a minimal dev panel); the Intent architecture with `HumanController`, `BotController` and `ScriptController`.\n1716\t*Done when:* a human can play a goal-scoring match against the CPU that already feels good; the physics unit tests\n1717\tpass (§11.3).\n1718\t\n1719\t**M2 — Characters and animation (risky; early).** Engine changes §5.2 (kit patterns) and §5.3 (tilt); the clip set\n1720\tcut and loaded; every animation row of §8.3 for outfield players and keepers; kits for all 6 teams.\n1721\t*Done when:* filmstrips of the pass, the shot, the slide, the launched victim, the keeper's low and high dives, the\n1722\theader, the bicycle kick, the dive and 3 celebrations look right (§11.7).\n1723\t\n1724\t**M3 — The rest of football.** Air moves (§6.5), skill moves (§6.6), defending (§6.7), keepers in full (§6.8), the\n1725\trules machine (§6.12: the clock, stoppage, halves, extra time, the shootout), set pieces (§6.11), the referee, fouls,\n1726\tadvantage, cards, theatrics and VAR (§6.10).\n1727\t*Done when:* the rules and set-piece tests pass, and an AI-versus-AI match produces corners, free kicks, cards and\n1728\tpenalties.\n1729\t\n1730\t**M4 — Team AI and balance.** TeamBrains with formations, tactics and gimmicks (§6.13, §7.1); difficulty; the AI overlay\n1731\tin dev mode; the soak test (§11.4) tuned to its targets.\n1732\t*Done when:* 20 seeded AI-versus-AI matches per tactic pair meet the soak targets.\n1733\t\n1734\t**M5 — The over-the-top layer.** Euphoria, Europhoria, Super Strikes (all 7 paths), the Save Duel (§6.9); the bus;\n1735\tcelebrations (§6.21); cinematics.\n1736\t*Done when:* every super strike's test passes and the Save Duel's timing windows are exact.\n1737\t\n1738\t**M6 — Presentation.** The 6 stadiums (§7.2) with stands, skylines, lights and weather (§6.19); the crowd view and mood\n1739\t(§6.18); matchday events (§6.20); replays (§6.15); the HUD in full (§6.16); the commentary director and its lines\n1740\t(§6.17, §7.4); audio in full: songs, SFX, the crowd engine, chants, babble voices (§6.22, engine changes §5.1, §5.4,\n1741\t§5.5).\n1742\t*Done when:* screenshots of each stadium at its time of day look right, and the audio smoke test plays without\n1743\terrors.\n1744\t\n1745\t**M7 — Front end and 10-foot UI.** The UI kit (§6.23), glyphs and prompts (§2.3), title, Kick-About setup with the\n1746\tcontroller side picker (§6.27), results, settings integration (§6.31), touch-only (§6.33), About (§6.32).\n1747\t*Done when:* every screen can be used with a pad only, a keyboard only, and a mouse only (scripted UI tests, §11.3).\n1748\t\n1749\t**M8 — The Cup Run.** The beat player and its step kinds, tabloids, the travel map, team talks, challenges, stickers,\n1750\tthe album, saves, the ending with the ceremony, the parade and the credits (§6.24, §7.3, §7.5).\n1751\t*Done when:* the scripted full playthrough passes (§11.5).\n1752\t\n1753\t**M9 — Training and Penalties.** The 9 drills (§6.25, §7.6) and Penalties mode (§6.26).\n1754\t*Done when:* each drill's scripted solve passes.\n1755\t\n1756\t**M10 — Attract and dev mode.** The idle watcher and the attract director (§6.29); dev mode in full (§6.30).\n1757\t*Done when:* the attract tests pass (it starts at 10.0 s, shows every segment, and any input exits) and every WARP\n1758\tentry runs without errors.\n1759\t\n1760\t**M11 — AI Hub online.** §6.28 in full; the fake-hub loopback tests (§11.6), then the real harness in Chromium.\n1761\t*Done when:* `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true for 2 players, for 4 players with latency 150, jitter 50 and loss 5,\n1762\tfor the host-leave scenario, and for the server scenario.\n1763\t\n1764\t**M12 — Bundle, polish, hand-back.** The final build; the full test pass; the look notes from `tools/check.mjs` acted\n1765\ton; screenshots reviewed; `exit-interview.json` written and validated; the About pages generated from it; the chat\n1766\treply (§12).\n1767\t\n1768\t---\n1769\t\n1770\t## 10. Risks and how to de-risk them\n1771\t\n1772\t| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n1773\t|---|---|---|\n1774\t| **Football-specific animation** (keeper dives, bicycle kicks, diving headers, dives) | The rig has no such moves; a bad dive ruins the game's look | M2 is early. Build the tilt state first, on one rig, in a test scene (`#dev` with an animation gallery: every move on a loop, every view). Filmstrip each move. Fallbacks: the built-in `flip` roll and `down`, sideways `Dodge_*_RM`, `Dive_Roll` from CMU |\n1775\t| **Kit patterns in the engine's torso painter** | It is drawn code inside the rig | A self-contained change behind `o.kit`; fallback: solid shirts with trim and no numbers (§5.2) |\n1776\t| **AI quality with 10 players** | Bad AI makes matches dull or broken: clumps, stuck players, no shots | A parametric formation model and utility scoring (§6.13), not ad hoc rules; the AI overlay; the soak test with numeric targets (§11.4) from M4 on |\n1777\t| **The feel of ball control** | Sticky ball versus loose ball; passes that miss | Dev sliders from M1; unit tests for pass accuracy; play it often from M1 |\n1778\t| **Netcode under latency and loss** | Shared-world football has a contested ball | Host authority with interpolation, input counters that survive loss, and the rate budget (§6.28, Appendix B). The sim/presentation split is in place from M1. Build a loopback fake hub with latency, jitter and loss in Node first (§11.6), then the real harness |\n1779\t| **Hub protocol details** (the card, ready, server mode, time-up, end) | The hub keeps a game that fails its check out of sessions | Follow the README's checklist line by line; run the harness's automatic check for every scenario it lists (§11.6) |\n1780\t| **Audio synthesis** (the crowd and babble) | WebAudio code is easy to get wrong, and silent in tests | One audio smoke page (`#dev` → sound test: every SFX, song, chant and voice on a list); headless no-ops tested; one screenshot-free check that no audio errors reach `game.errors` |\n1781\t| **Many systems, one IIFE** | Name clashes, load-order bugs | Numbered fragments with one namespace; the content validator; the full playthrough test |\n1782\t| **Scope** | It is a lot of game | Data-driven content; the milestone order puts the core first; each milestone ends playable. The list in §12 is the scope: build all of it, but do the core well before the extras are polished |\n1783\t| **Determinism** (tests and replays) | `Math.random` in sim code breaks proofs | A lint test greps `src/` for `Math.random` outside cosmetic code; the determinism test (§11.4) |\n1784\t| **Bundle correctness** | `</script>` in inlined code; the order of hub metas and `session.js` | The build checks both; a test parses the deliverable's `<head>` order (§11.8) |\n1785\t\n1786\t---\n1787\t\n1788\t## 11. Testing\n1789\t\n1790\t### 11.1 The one command\n1791\t\n1792\t`node tools/test.mjs` runs every suite and prints **only failures** (one line each: `FAIL <suite> <test>: <detail>`) and\n1793\tone last line: `Europhoria tests: <passed> passed, <failed> failed (<seconds> s)`. It exits with 1 on any failure.\n1794\t`node tools/test.mjs <suite> [...]` runs only the named suites, so after a change you rerun only the suites that cover"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"9eca6c66-8849-4edb-a442-cc89add0a71e","uuid":"cd63b366-bfbc-4d0a-b6a2-156ccad866b6","timestamp":"2026-11-04T01:32:30.774Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/home/micha/dev/cc-matrix/runs/claude-opus-5-5-max.plan__20261103-174834__x4394d1/work/PLAN.md","content":"- **The tabloid page, the travel map, the bracket cards, the sticker frames:** UI art in code.\n- **Weather and pyro overlays:** fog layers, flare smoke, confetti, fireworks (particles).\n\nFrom the engine's library (generic props, `node tools/asset-find.mjs`): benches (`bench`, `kenney-holiday:bench`) for\nthe dugouts and the training ground; `lamppost` and `kenney-graveyard:lightpost-double` on the harbour road; `fence`\nand `kenney-fantasy-town:hedge` at the rec ground; `kenney-holiday:snowman` outside the Stahlpresse Arena;\n`kenney-fantasy-town:stall-red` market stalls (the pie stand, the Kipperton harbour); `kenney-pirate:flag` on the\ntrawler; palms (`r.prop('palm')`) at Solera; `crate`, `barrel` and `sign` at the harbour. Load an asset set with its\nscript before `game.js` and `E.addAssets(window.ASSETS['kenney-holiday'])`, or cut the few entries the game uses into\na set of its own with `tools/asset-set.mjs`.\n\n### 8.3 Animation\n\nThree sources, all on the engine's Humanoid rig: (a) the engine's own animation (gait from velocity, `E.MOVES`-style\nattack specs, poses, expressions); (b) mocap clips through `Mocap.drive(rig, lib)` (set `rig.mocap` each step,\n`rig.mocapW` to fade, `rig.mocapMask = 'upper'` for the arms over the legs); (c) procedural recipes: the tilt state\n(§5.3) and joint post-processing (wrap `rig.solvePose`, as the API card shows).\n\n**Cut the clip set** (run in the scratch clone of the engine repository):\n\n```sh\nnode tools/anim-set.mjs src/mocap/sets/quaternius.js src/mocap/sets/mesh2motion.js src/mocap/sets/cmu.js \\\n  examples/cmu-lib/CMU_10.js examples/cmu-lib/CMU_11.js \\\n  --clips \"QUATERNIUS:Slide_Start,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Loop,QUATERNIUS:Slide_Exit,QUATERNIUS:Hit_Knockback,QUATERNIUS:LayToIdle,QUATERNIUS:OverhandThrow,QUATERNIUS:Roll,Victory,Cheer_One_arm,Cheering_Two_Hands,Dance_Simple,Angry,Backflip,Help_Two_Arms,Death_C,Dodge_left,Dodge_right,Greeting,Cartwheel,Jump_Twist,Breakdance_Helicopter,Shrug,Fall_On_Face,Get_Up_Face_Down,Get_Up_From_Back,Get_Up_From_Side,Run_Quick_Stop,Wave_Hello,10_02,10_05,11_01\" \\\n  --name EF --title \"Europhoria Football\" --out <dev folder>/mocap/ef-clips.js \\\n  --credit \"Quaternius Universal Animation Library 1 and 2 (CC0); Mesh2Motion (CC0); CMU Graphics Lab Motion Capture Database (mocap.cs.cmu.edu), free for all uses; created with funding from NSF EIA-0196217.\"\n```\n\nIf a name is in more than one set, the tool says so: prefix it `SET:`. If a clip's name differs, check the set's\ncatalog (`src/mocap/catalogs/*.json`) and fix the list. Expect about 150–250 KB. The CMU soccer takes play only a\nwindow around the kick: find the contact time once (the frame where the right foot's forward reach peaks), store it in\n`EF.Anim.CLIPS`, and sample from `contact − 0.45 s` to `contact + 0.35 s`.\n\n| Moment | Source | How |\n|---|---|---|\n| idle, jog, run, sprint | engine | the gait from velocity; `sprint: true` adds the lean |\n| dribble touch | engine spec | `touch: { rel, kick: true, a0: .2, a1: 0, z0: .08, z1: .12, reach: 4, wind: .03, active: .04, recover: .08 }` every stride |\n| pass | engine spec | `pass: { rel, kick: true, a0: .6, a1: -.1, z0: .15, z1: .2, reach: 6, wind: .08, active: .08, recover: .16, twist: .4 }` (inside foot) |\n| shot | spec, plus mocap for power ≥ .8 | `shot: { rel, kick: true, a0: .05, a1: 0, z0: .3, z1: 1.1, reach: 7, wind: .12, active: .1, recover: .26, lean: -.25, lunge: 2 }`; at high power blend `10_02`'s kick window in over the spec (`mocapW` 1, then fading to 0 in the recovery) |\n| penalty run-up and kick | mocap | `11_01` (the run-up and kick), with root motion supplied by the body |\n| chip / lob | spec | `chip: { a0: .1, a1: 0, z0: .1, z1: 1.4, reach: 5.5, lean: -.4 }` |\n| volley | spec | `volley: { a0: .4, a1: -.2, z0: .9, z1: 1.2, reach: 7, hop: 2, lean: -.4, twist: .6 }` |\n| header | procedural | `air: true` with a z arc; tilt forward 20° (axis `right`); the head snaps forward at contact (post-process `J.head`) |\n| diving header | procedural | tilt +75° about `right` (pivot hips, lift 6), arms back; lands with `down` 0.5 s; up with `Get_Up_Face_Down` |\n| bicycle kick | procedural | tilt −140° about `right` (pivot hips, lift up to 14 at contact), with `axekick`-style kick: `{ kick: true, a0: .1, a1: 0, z0: 2.2, z1: 1.5, reach: 6 }`; lands on the back (`down`); up with `Get_Up_From_Back` |\n| slide tackle | mocap | `Slide_Start` → `Slide_Loop` → `Slide_Exit` (the body supplies the travel) |\n| poke tackle | spec | `poke: { kick: true, a0: .3, a1: 0, z0: .1, z1: .1, reach: 7.5, lunge: 3, wind: .05, active: .08, recover: .15 }` |\n| barge | engine move | `bash`, with a lean |\n| launched by a slide | procedural | tilt about `forward` spinning 1.5 turns over 0.6 s while the body flies (vz 120), stars; then `down: 1`; up with `LayToIdle` or `Get_Up_From_Side` |\n| knocked back | mocap | `Hit_Knockback`, then `LayToIdle` |\n| wrong-footed | mocap | `Dodge_left` / `Dodge_right` at `mocapW` .7, with `hurt` |\n| step-over | spec | two quick `kick` specs sweeping across the ball (`a0` from ±.9 to ∓.3), 0.15 s apart |\n| spin turn | engine | `rig.spin` from 0 to 2π over 0.45 s |\n| rainbow flick | spec | heel flick: `{ kick: true, a0: 3.0, a1: 2.6, z0: .1, z1: 1.3, reach: 4 }` (behind, upward) |\n| skid stop | mocap | `Run_Quick_Stop` (upper body, `mocapMask: 'upper'`) on hard stops |\n| theatrical dive | procedural + mocap | launch forward (tilt +80° about `right`, lift 8), land, 2 sideways rolls (tilt about `forward` spinning 2 turns while sliding 30), lie clutching a shin (`down: 1`, `expr: 'wince'`, hands to `J.kneeR`); if booked, up with `Shrug` |\n| protests | mocap | `Angry`, `Help_Two_Arms`, `Shrug` (upper) |\n| tired | procedural | lean 30°, hands to the knees (post-process `J.handL`/`J.handR` toward `J.kneeL`/`J.kneeR`) at stoppages when stamina is under 25 |\n| keeper set | engine | `pose: 'guard'`, crouch .3 |\n| keeper dive | procedural | tilt ±(70–95)° about `forward` (pivot feet), lifted 2 (low) to 14 (high) on an arc; lateral speed 260 easing to 0; hands IK'd (`E.ik3`) to the ball's point; then `down` on the side; up with `Get_Up_From_Side` |\n| keeper catch / parry / tip | procedural / engine | hands to the chest (catch); `jab` toward the ball (parry); one arm up with a jump (tip) |\n| keeper throw | mocap | `OverhandThrow`; an underarm roll as a spec with the arm low |\n| smother | procedural | a low forward dive (tilt +80° about `right`, lift 2) |\n| celebrations | mocap + procedural | knee slide: `Slide_Loop` with arms out (post-process); `Backflip`; `Cartwheel`; aeroplane: run with the arms horizontal (post-process) and a lean into the turn; robot: `Dance_Simple` at 0.6× speed with the arms bent square (post-process); shirt over head: `hood: true` with the hood in the shirt colour plus `Cheering_Two_Hands`; corner-flag dance: `Dance_Simple`; badge kiss: `Greeting`; helicopter: `Breakdance_Helicopter`; fish slap: two players face each other, alternating `jab` with a kipper sprite in the hand; pile-on: teammates `Victory` / `Cheer_One_arm` |\n| referee | engine + procedural | whistle (hand to mouth), points to the spot (`point: true`), the card raised high (hand above the head; the card sprite at `rig.hand('R')`), advantage (both arms forward), the VAR rectangle (both hands trace a box), hand to the ear; knocked over by the ball (`Fall_On_Face`, then up) |\n| manager | mocap | pacing (gait), `Angry` (conceding), `Victory` (scoring), `Help_Two_Arms` (instructions), `Cheering_Two_Hands` |\n| tunnel and handshakes | engine + procedural | a walk; an arm forward (`point: true`) as the lines pass |\n| crowd front rows | engine | classic-style rigs with `pose: 'cheer'`, `wave`, arms down for boos |\n\nCheck every attack and every procedural move with `tools/filmstrip.mjs` (§11.7): a wind-up, a strike, and a settle\nwithout jerks or backward sweeps.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Build order and milestones\n\nEach milestone ends with its tests passing (`node tools/test.mjs`), the build working, and a short note in the dev\nfolder's `PROGRESS.md`. Do them in order: each one builds on the last, and the risky parts come early.\n\n**M0 — Setup (½ day).** The dev folder; the engine copied; `vendor/` filled; `package.json`; `tools/build.mjs`\nproducing `build/game.js`, the dev page and the deliverable; `tools/test.mjs` with its vm loader and one smoke test;\n`kits/sports.js` running as `src/` fragments, unchanged, through the pipeline (proof: its `run(600)` hash is the same\ntwice).\n*Done when:* `node tools/build.mjs && node tools/test.mjs` passes, and `node tools/check.mjs` on the deliverable shows\nthe kit's cage match.\n\n**M1 — The football sandbox (the feel).** The broadcast view; the pitch geometry and TileMap (§6.1); the ball (§6.2);\n5-a-side footballers with movement, stamina and dribbling (§6.3); pass, through, lob, one-two (§6.4); shooting with\nthe meter, sweet spot, aim, curl and chip (§6.5, without air moves); possession; goals; kickoffs; a temporary formation\nAI (the kit's, widened to 5); the camera director (§6.14); the score bug and power meter; `EF.T` with the TUNE tab only\n(a minimal dev panel); the Intent architecture with `HumanController`, `BotController` and `ScriptController`.\n*Done when:* a human can play a goal-scoring match against the CPU that already feels good; the physics unit tests\npass (§11.3).\n\n**M2 — Characters and animation (risky; early).** Engine changes §5.2 (kit patterns) and §5.3 (tilt); the clip set\ncut and loaded; every animation row of §8.3 for outfield players and keepers; kits for all 6 teams.\n*Done when:* filmstrips of the pass, the shot, the slide, the launched victim, the keeper's low and high dives, the\nheader, the bicycle kick, the dive and 3 celebrations look right (§11.7).\n\n**M3 — The rest of football.** Air moves (§6.5), skill moves (§6.6), defending (§6.7), keepers in full (§6.8), the\nrules machine (§6.12: the clock, stoppage, halves, extra time, the shootout), set pieces (§6.11), the referee, fouls,\nadvantage, cards, theatrics and VAR (§6.10).\n*Done when:* the rules and set-piece tests pass, and an AI-versus-AI match produces corners, free kicks, cards and\npenalties.\n\n**M4 — Team AI and balance.** TeamBrains with formations, tactics and gimmicks (§6.13, §7.1); difficulty; the AI overlay\nin dev mode; the soak test (§11.4) tuned to its targets.\n*Done when:* 20 seeded AI-versus-AI matches per tactic pair meet the soak targets.\n\n**M5 — The over-the-top layer.** Euphoria, Europhoria, Super Strikes (all 7 paths), the Save Duel (§6.9); the bus;\ncelebrations (§6.21); cinematics.\n*Done when:* every super strike's test passes and the Save Duel's timing windows are exact.\n\n**M6 — Presentation.** The 6 stadiums (§7.2) with stands, skylines, lights and weather (§6.19); the crowd view and mood\n(§6.18); matchday events (§6.20); replays (§6.15); the HUD in full (§6.16); the commentary director and its lines\n(§6.17, §7.4); audio in full: songs, SFX, the crowd engine, chants, babble voices (§6.22, engine changes §5.1, §5.4,\n§5.5).\n*Done when:* screenshots of each stadium at its time of day look right, and the audio smoke test plays without\nerrors.\n\n**M7 — Front end and 10-foot UI.** The UI kit (§6.23), glyphs and prompts (§2.3), title, Kick-About setup with the\ncontroller side picker (§6.27), results, settings integration (§6.31), touch-only (§6.33), About (§6.32).\n*Done when:* every screen can be used with a pad only, a keyboard only, and a mouse only (scripted UI tests, §11.3).\n\n**M8 — The Cup Run.** The beat player and its step kinds, tabloids, the travel map, team talks, challenges, stickers,\nthe album, saves, the ending with the ceremony, the parade and the credits (§6.24, §7.3, §7.5).\n*Done when:* the scripted full playthrough passes (§11.5).\n\n**M9 — Training and Penalties.** The 9 drills (§6.25, §7.6) and Penalties mode (§6.26).\n*Done when:* each drill's scripted solve passes.\n\n**M10 — Attract and dev mode.** The idle watcher and the attract director (§6.29); dev mode in full (§6.30).\n*Done when:* the attract tests pass (it starts at 10.0 s, shows every segment, and any input exits) and every WARP\nentry runs without errors.\n\n**M11 — AI Hub online.** §6.28 in full; the fake-hub loopback tests (§11.6), then the real harness in Chromium.\n*Done when:* `window.__hubCheck.pass` is true for 2 players, for 4 players with latency 150, jitter 50 and loss 5,\nfor the host-leave scenario, and for the server scenario.\n\n**M12 — Bundle, polish, hand-back.** The final build; the full test pass; the look notes from `tools/check.mjs` acted\non; screenshots reviewed; `exit-interview.json` written and validated; the About pages generated from it; the chat\nreply (§12).\n\n---\n\n## 10. Risks and how to de-risk them\n\n| Risk | Why it is risky | De-risk |\n|---|---|---|\n| **Football-specific animation** (keeper dives, bicycle kicks, diving headers, dives) | The rig has no such moves; a bad dive ruins the game's look | M2 is early. Build the tilt state first, on one rig, in a test scene (`#dev` with an animation gallery: every move on a loop, every view). Filmstrip each move. Fallbacks: the built-in `flip` roll and `down`, sideways `Dodge_*_RM`, `Dive_Roll` from CMU |\n| **Kit patterns in the engine's torso painter** | It is drawn code inside the rig | A self-contained change behind `o.kit`; fallback: solid shirts with trim and no numbers (§5.2) |\n| **AI quality with 10 players** | Bad AI makes matches dull or broken: clumps, stuck players, no shots | A parametric formation model and utility scoring (§6.13), not ad hoc rules; the AI overlay; the soak test with numeric targets (§11.4) from M4 on |\n| **The feel of ball control** | Sticky ball versus loose ball; passes that miss | Dev sliders from M1; unit tests for pass accuracy; play it often from M1 |\n| **Netcode under latency and loss** | Shared-world football has a contested ball | Host authority with interpolation, input counters that survive loss, and the rate budget (§6.28, Appendix B). The sim/presentation split is in place from M1. Build a loopback fake hub with latency, jitter and loss in Node first (§11.6), then the real harness |\n| **Hub protocol details** (the card, ready, server mode, time-up, end) | The hub keeps a game that fails its check out of sessions | Follow the README's checklist line by line; run the harness's automatic check for every scenario it lists (§11.6) |\n| **Audio synthesis** (the crowd and babble) | WebAudio code is easy to get wrong, and silent in tests | One audio smoke page (`#dev` → sound test: every SFX, song, chant and voice on a list); headless no-ops tested; one screenshot-free check that no audio errors reach `game.errors` |\n| **Many systems, one IIFE** | Name clashes, load-order bugs | Numbered fragments with one namespace; the content validator; the full playthrough test |\n| **Scope** | It is a lot of game | Data-driven content; the milestone order puts the core first; each milestone ends playable. The list in §12 is the scope: build all of it, but do the core well before the extras are polished |\n| **Determinism** (tests and replays) | `Math.random` in sim code breaks proofs | A lint test greps `src/` for `Math.random` outside cosmetic code; the determinism test (§11.4) |\n| **Bundle correctness** | `</script>` in inlined code; the order of hub metas and `session.js` | The build checks both; a test parses the deliverable's `<head>` order (§11.8) |\n\n---\n\n## 11. Testing\n\n### 11.1 The one command\n\n`node tools/test.mjs` runs every suite and prints **only failures** (one line each: `FAIL <suite> <test>: <detail>`) and\none last line: `Europhoria tests: <passed> passed, <failed> failed (<seconds> s)`. It exits with 1 on any failure.\n`node tools/test.mjs <suite> [...]` runs only the named suites, so after a change you rerun only the suites that cover","numLines":170,"startLine":1625,"totalLines":2146}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_01NA1xtZFoz4zj527Ae1YXgB","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
